  "as_of": "2014-11-26",
  "sentences": [
   "The bill would change membership and functions of Parliament House's Security Management Board by adding federal police representation and expressly covering the operation of security measures.",
   "The Australian Federal Police Commissioner could serve on the board, or the presiding officers could nominate a deputy commissioner or senior executive employee instead.",
   "The amendments would begin the day after royal assent and operate through two changes to the board's existing provisions in the Parliamentary Service Act."
  ],
  "changes": [
   "The board's membership provisions would expressly include the federal police commissioner.",
   "Presiding officers could select a senior federal police representative as an alternative to the commissioner.",
   "The board's statutory remit would expand to cover operational security measures."
  ],
  "affected": "The Security Management Board, Australian Federal Police leadership and the presiding officers are affected.",
